    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cca66ca7_a37b58c8",
        "filename": "driver/ppc/syv682x.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 624,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-13T20:30:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The main thing is if the SYV682 is acting as a sink, we have to be very careful about changes to Control Register 1.  The failure we saw earlier in the Volteer project was a board brown-out because there was no battery connected and the EC was reset (either from a FW update, sysjump, or manual reset).\n\nI think this is a good change, so that syv682x_vbus_sink_enable() is responsible for setting HV_ILIM.",
      "parentUuid": "220a29ce_1e505cbd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 624,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 624,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "1ba06624531b55bd05bd27af815d8eaacb8a7b4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae224e7a_2270c416",
        "filename": "driver/ppc/syv682x.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 624,
      "author": {
        "id": 1176029
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-14T01:58:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we move the setting of HV_ILIM into syv682x_vbus_sink_enable then it turns out that no matter codes go to IF or ELSE, HV_ILIM will always be configured in the init function?\n\nWill it hit the problem you mentioned?",
      "parentUuid": "cca66ca7_a37b58c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 624,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 624,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "1ba06624531b55bd05bd27af815d8eaacb8a7b4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2c6c983_387bc062",
        "filename": "driver/ppc/syv682x.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 624,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-14T22:02:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting HV_ILIM in the sink enable routine does make the setting here during init() not strictly needed.  Especially because the code here is turning off all the power paths.  I think it\u0027s useful to have the HV_ILIM set here for debug purposes as it makes it easier to verify the setting prior to connected an external SRC.",
      "parentUuid": "ae224e7a_2270c416",
